Description: Drop the rstest dev-dependency
 `rstest` is only used by the integration tests in tests/run.rs, it is never
 compiled by the Debian build (`dh_auto_test` runs `python3 -m unittest
 discover`, and setup.py only builds the `maturin` binary).  However
 `debian/rules` regenerates Cargo.lock with `cargo generate-lockfile
 --offline`, and cargo resolves the complete dependency graph, dev-dependencies
 included.  UOS 25 therefore has to ship `librust-rstest-dev`, which in turn
 depends on `librust-futures-timer-3+default-dev`, a crate that does not exist
 in UOS 25 at all.
 .
 Dropping the dev-dependency removes that whole chain, so `rust-futures-timer`
 no longer has to be submitted either.  The two rstest-parametrised tests are
 rewritten as plain `#[test]` functions that iterate over the same cases, so
 the test suite still builds and covers the same ground.
Author: lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
